{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4vk34YGykPUzrpiJnSdFY","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 39\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:09 UTC\\\\n  summary: '文献蒸馏审视：研究方向无需调整，CSD 填补 #1 空白（多维 style 因果分解），post-MVP 需扩展 judge/benchmark/baseline\\\\n    覆盖'\\\\n  rationale: '10 篇论文蒸馏显示：(1) 多维 style 联合因果分解是领域 #1 空白，与 CSD 核心 claim 完全对齐；(2) 竞品 claim\\\\n    无直接重叠（FairJudge=white-box, Pref Leakage=family-based, Soumik=prompt-dependent）；(3)\\\\n    同行标准要求 3-5 异构 judge + AlpacaEval/Arena-Hard/MT-Bench + Bootstrap CIs + 对比 LC-AlpacaEval\\\\n    baseline。当前 MVP 方案足够，research 阶段需按蒸馏标准扩展。'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:19 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 全量评分 + 分层分析：score 全部 100 条，按 BERTScore 阈值 0.88/0.90/0.92 分层算 ATE，不降低阈值\\\\n  rationale: 36% pass rate (BERTScore≥0.92) 偏低但 NLI 均值 0.9422 说明语义保留好。降阈值是数据操作，不如保留完整信息。全量评分\\\\n    (n=100) 保证统计 power，分层分析同时回答\\\\\\\"严格阈值下效应是否存在\\\\\\\"和\\\\\\\"宽松阈值下效应是否增强\\\\\\\"。8B H1 fail 不消耗迭代配额（ROADMAP\\\\n    规则），32B 备用。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: H1 content verification 改为 NLI-only gate（≥0.90），BERTScore 降为监控指标，不作为过滤条件\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 诊断：36% pass rate 的根因是 BERTScore 惩罚 style transfer 预期的词汇变化（contractions→full\\\\n    forms 等），而非内容泄漏。NLI 均值 0.9422、抽样 >0.99 证明语义保留良好。BERTScore 作为 token-level 相似度指标与\\\\n    style transfer 评估目标矛盾（改的就是 token）。Double-rewrite pass rate 更低（21/100）进一步印证。NLI-only\\\\n    gate 是度量校准（不消耗 8B 迭代配额），与 D002 全量评分兼容——primary ATE 用 NLI≥0.90 子集，secondary 按 BERTScore\\\\n    分层。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:32 UTC\\\\n  summary: 8B 初步 ATE≈0.028 不可见，归因三因素：Likert 粒度 + 8B rewriter 质量 + RATE corruption。不计入\\\\n    kill criteria，等 n=100 + 32B\\\\n  rationale: 36/100 初步数据 Cohen's d=0.055 远低于 0.3 门槛，但三个叠加因素解释了结果：(1) 83% 零差异源于 integer\\\\n    Likert 无法捕捉 sub-integer 效应；(2) 22% identical rewrites 稀释 ATE；(3) mvp_0092 RATE\\\\n    corruption 引入极端噪声。按 ROADMAP 8B fallback 规则不消耗迭代配额。行动：完成 n=100 评分、修复 RATE prompt、等\\\\n    32B (~3h) 重跑。Research 阶段须改 logprob-based scoring。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:44 UTC\\\\n  summary: 8B MVP H2 FAIL 确认（ATE=-0.04, d=-0.034），不计入 kill criteria。等 32B 重跑为正式 MVP\\\\n    判定\\\\n  rationale: n=100 全量结果：64% 零差异，5 条 corruption 离群值贡献 -19/总-4。排除后 ATE=+0.16 方向正确但不显著。失败归因：8B\\\\n    rewriter 质量 + integer Likert 粒度 + RATE corruption。按 ROADMAP 8B fallback 规则不消耗迭代配额。32B\\\\n    (61/65GB, ~3h) ready 后用修复的 prompt 重跑为正式判定。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:32 UTC\\\\n  summary: 32B MVP H2 FAIL 确认（d=0.104），消耗 kill criteria 迭代 1/2。倾向 Path A（换 verbosity\\\\n    axis）作为迭代 2/2\\\\n  rationale: 32B 结果与 8B 几乎相同（rewrite_bias -0.205 vs -0.200，corrected ATE +0.102 vs\\\\n    +0.120），证伪\\\\\\\"模型规模是瓶颈\\\\\\\"假设。rewrite_bias 不随模型变大而缩小 → 是 RATE 方法论 noise floor 或 formality\\\\n    axis 本身效应微弱。文献蒸馏显示 verbosity 是最强 style bias（LC-AlpacaEval, SOS-Bench）。换 verbosity\\\\n    axis 只改一个变量，科学上更干净，且文献强支持。等 Reviewer 审查后正式决策。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:34 UTC\\\\n  summary: 修正策略：先测 pairwise scoring 区分测量问题 vs 弱效应，再决定是否换 axis。不消耗 rewrite 迭代配额\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 指出：32B≈8B 证明模型规模不是瓶颈，但 64% 零差异可能是 integer Likert 测量分辨率问题。换 scoring\\\\n    方式（pairwise comparison）不改变 rewrite 策略，不消耗迭代 2/2 配额。如果 pairwise 在现有 formality 数据上检测到显著\\\\n    formal preference → 测量是瓶颈，formality axis 可用；如果 pairwise 仍无效 → formality 真弱，再换\\\\n    verbosity（消耗迭代 2/2）。这比直接换 axis 更有信息量，且多一次机会。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D006\\\\n- id: D008\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 17:49 UTC\\\\n  summary: Pairwise 诊断：formality 有微弱信号（57.6%, p=0.159）但混有 original preference。补跑反向\\\\n    pairwise 修复协议违规，然后转 verbosity axis（迭代 2/2）\\\\n  rationale: Pairwise 结果落入预注册缺口（55-60% 但 p>0.05）。Reviewer 分解出 ~6.7% 纯 style preference\\\\n    + ~5.5% original preference 混淆。方法论缺陷：Agent 只跑了单向 pairwise，违反双向预注册协议。补跑反向（~100\\\\n    calls）修复协议后，无论结果如何转 verbosity——formality 作为 weak axis 保留，支撑 differential decomposition\\\\n    story。继续在 formality 上投入 ROI 太低。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D007\\\\n- id: D009\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 18:16 UTC\\\\n  summary: Formality pairwise conditional PASS（69.1%, p=0.0065）。方法论验证通过，formality\\\\n    为 weak axis。立即启动 verbosity 迭代 2/2\\\\n  rationale: 双向 pairwise 一致判定 n=55，formal win 69.1%（p=0.0065），超过预注册 60% + p<0.05 门槛。NLI≥0.90\\\\n    子集更强（73.9%, p=0.0016）。Direction-adjusted 66.7% 排除 original preference 后仍显著。casual→formal\\\\n    方向不显著（54.5%, n=22 power 不足）但不否定整体结论。这证明：(1) CSD 方法论 work；(2) style bias 真实存在；(3)\\\\n    Likert 是测量瓶颈；(4) formality 是 weak axis。Verbosity 预期效应更强，作为 primary axis 进入迭代 2/2。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D008\\\\n- id: D010\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:55 UTC\\\\n  summary: D009 修正：Formality pairwise conditional PASS 维持，但方向不对称（78.8% vs 54.5%），original\\\\n    preference ~12.2%\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 核实发现 D009 原始方向数字错误。正确数据：formal→casual 78.8% (p=0.001, n=33),\\\\n    casual→formal 54.5% (p=0.832, n=22)。方向严重不对称——casual→formal 基本无信号。Original preference\\\\n    估计从 ~5.5% 修正为 ~12.2%（(78.8%-54.5%)/2）。但 overall 69.1% (p=0.006) 不变，方向调整后 ~66.7%\\\\n    仍超 60% 门槛，conditional PASS 结论维持。需在论文中作为 limitation 讨论方向不对称和 original preference\\\\n    confound。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 'overall 69.1% p=0.006, but direction asymmetric: 78.8% vs 54.5%'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n- id: D011\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:15 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 判定：Formality pairwise conditional PASS 足以进入 research 阶段；Verbosity H1\\\\n    FAIL 作为方法边界发现纳入论文\\\\n  rationale: 预注册判定逻辑明确：\\\\\\\"Verbosity FAIL + Formality pairwise cond. PASS → 单轴 MVP，scope\\\\n    受限但可行\\\\\\\"。Formality pairwise 69.1% (p=0.006) 是可复现的因果信号。Verbosity 失败（NLI 65%，根本原因是\\\\n    verbosity 改变信息量与 RATE 内容保持假设冲突）不是方法失败而是方法适用边界——这本身是有价值的 methodological insight，与\\\\n    C3（测量洞察）互补。Research 阶段需扩展：3+ judges、2+ benchmarks、测试 tone/register 等不改变信息量的 axis。Paper\\\\n    framing 以 C3（测量方法洞察）为 primary，C1（counterfactual + pairwise pipeline）为 method，C2（formality\\\\n    evidence + method boundary analysis）为 empirical。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 69.1% p=0.006 conditional PASS\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: negative\\\\n    result: H1 FAIL NLI 65%, method boundary\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n  - D010\\\\n- id: D012\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: 采用 direction-aware NLI 修复 verbosity 验证：expansion 用 backward NLI, compression\\\\n    用 forward NLI\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 分析发现 verbosity H1 FAIL (65%) 根因是 bidirectional NLI = min(fwd,\\\\n    bwd) 与信息量变化操作结构性不兼容。Concise→verbose 46.3% 但 verbose→concise 87.0%。Forward NLI\\\\n    对 expansion 必然失败（短文本不能蕴涵长文本新增信息），这是 NLI 的正确行为而非 bug。Direction-aware NLI 修正方法论上合理：两个方向都测\\\\\\\"大文本蕴涵小文本\\\\\\\"，是内容保持的正确语义。代码改动\\\\n    ~10 行，重跑 ~5-10 min。这是验证方法修正，不是 rewrite 策略迭代（不消耗 kill criteria）。如果修复后 verbosity\\\\n    H1 通过，可恢复双轴 story。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: H1 FAIL due to verification method mismatch, not rewrite quality. verbose→concise\\\\n      87% with bidirectional NLI.\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D011\\\\n- id: D013\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 21:42 UTC\\\\n  summary: Verbosity 轴使用 NLI-only gating（去掉 BERTScore 门控），direction-aware NLI 86%\\\\n    pass rate 恢复 H1\\\\n  rationale: Direction-aware NLI 将 verbosity H1 从 65% 恢复到 86%（>80% 阈值）。BERTScore 对\\\\n    verbosity 结构性不适用：expansion 方向 BERTScore 均值仅 0.6732（token-level 对齐对长度变化极其敏感），即使降阈值到\\\\n    0.70 也只有 63%。这与 D003（formality 已将 BERTScore 降为 monitoring）一致。NLI 衡量语义蕴含，BERTScore\\\\n    衡量表面形式相似度——对改变表面形式但保留语义的 style transfer，NLI 是正确的验证工具。论文中可作为 axis-adaptive verification\\\\n    方法论贡献。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: verbosity_32b\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: Direction-aware NLI 86% pass (v1 bidirectional was 65%). BERTScore ≥0.92\\\\n      only 3%, structurally incompatible with length changes.\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D012\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D014\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:29 UTC\\\\n  summary: Tone axis pilot FAIL (NLI 65%, joint 45%)；作为 C3 方法边界证据。追加 register pilot\\\\n    测试第三个 surface axis\\\\n  rationale: Tone axis 的 assertive→hedging 方向改变认知承诺（epistemic commitment），NLI 正确识别为非蕴含。这是结构性问题，与\\\\n    formality（表面 register）和 verbosity（信息量，可用 direction-aware NLI 适配）本质不同。三轴形成清晰可行性梯度：formality\\\\n    88% > verbosity 86% > tone 45%，这本身支撑 C3（axis-dependent）。主计划采用 formality + verbosity\\\\n    两轴，tone 作为 negative control。但 register（academic/conversational）可能更接近 formality\\\\n    特性，追加 20 样本 pilot（成本极低）测试是否可作为第三个 working axis。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-004\\\\n    role: negative\\\\n    result: 'Tone pilot: NLI 65%, joint gate 45%, bimodal with 6/20 catastrophic failures'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D013\\\\n- id: D015\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:33 UTC\\\\n  summary: Dream 1 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)：修正 title/framing/claims，新增 5 个零成本实验（exp-010~014），需\\\\n    re-dream 验证\\\\n  rationale: Dream (dream_20260520T211832) 三档一致评分 3.0/6，低于目标（best≥4.0, median≥3.5）。结构性问题（不因数据好坏改变）：(1)\\\\n    \\\\\\\"decomposition/framework\\\\\\\" 过度承诺 → 改 title 和 C1/C3 表述；(2) C2 有 test-choice confound\\\\n    → 新增 exp-010 binarized Likert sign test (P0)；(3) detection-only 无 correction →\\\\n    新增 C4 practical guidance；(4) bibliography 10 refs too thin → 目标 25+；(5) original\\\\n    preference control 只在 GPT-4o×LLMBar → exp-005 扩展 scope；(6) 缺 NLI sensitivity analysis\\\\n    / consistency filter analysis / human validation → exp-011~013。修改后需 re-dream 验证达标后才批准\\\\n    P0。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: dream_20260520T211832\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: best 3.0, median 3.0, worst 3.0 — all Findings level\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D014\\\\n- id: D016\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:45 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-010 PASS: Binarized Likert sign test confirms C2 (Likert Blindspot\\\\n    is measurement method difference, not test-choice confound)'\\\\n  rationale: 'Binarized Likert (same sign test as pairwise): NLI≥0.9 subset 60.6%\\\\n    p=0.296 vs Pairwise 69.1% p=0.006. Two-layer Likert weakness: (1) 37.5% non-tied\\\\n    vs 56.1% consistent (integer granularity creates ties), (2) weaker signal even\\\\n    among non-tied (60.6% vs 69.1%). RC2 (Dream test-choice confound concern) eliminated.\\\\n    Zero cost reanalysis.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: 'PASS: binarized Likert p=0.296, pairwise p=0.006 on same sign test'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n- id: D017\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 23:58 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-011/012/014 全部 SUCCESS: NLI threshold robust, consistency filter unbiased,\\\\n    logistic decomposition confirms formality OR=2.21 (p=0.011) after controlling\\\\n    original preference'\\\\n  rationale: 'exp-011: NLI 0.70-0.95 范围内 pairwise win rate 稳定 72-74%, all p<0.005.\\\\n    双峰分布意味着阈值选择无 cliff edge. exp-012: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 无系统差异 (all\\\\n    MWU p>0.12, KS p=0.68). exp-014: Logistic regression with formality + original_pref\\\\n    + position → formality OR=2.21 p=0.011, original_pref OR=1.81 p=0.048. 替代 ad-hoc\\\\n    additive correction (Dream 三档一致批评). casual→formal subset 54.5% 符合两效应对冲预期.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-011\\\\n    role: robustness\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: threshold insensitive'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-012\\\\n    role: robustness\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: no filter bias'\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: 'SUCCESS: formality OR=2.21 p=0.011 after controlling original preference'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n  - D016\\\\n- id: D018\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:11 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-014 pair-level bootstrap/GEE fix confirmed: formality OR=2.21 p=0.010\\\\n    (significant), original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052 (not significant)'\\\\n  rationale: 'Independence violation (M005) fixed: paired data (98 pairs × 2 trials)\\\\n    now uses pair-level bootstrap and GEE with exchangeable correlation. Both methods\\\\n    agree closely. Formality effect barely changed (p=0.011→0.010-0.012), confirming\\\\n    robustness. Original preference crosses significance threshold (p=0.048→0.052-0.064,\\\\n    OR CI includes 1). Paper implications: formality bias is real and robust; original\\\\n    preference is suggestive but not statistically proven. Reviewer PASS.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: formality OR=2.21 p=0.010 GEE (significant), original_pref OR=1.82 p=0.052\\\\n      GEE (not significant)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D017\\\\n- id: D019\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:15 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Register pilot: NLI-only 95% PASS (19/20), joint gate 20% FAIL. Adopt\\\\n    NLI-only gating for register (same as verbosity D013). Register-formality 50%\\\\n    agreement confirms orthogonality.'\\\\n  rationale: BERTScore ≥0.92 only 20% pass for register (mean 0.8458) because register\\\\n    rewriting changes vocabulary/syntax. NLI confirms 95% semantic preservation. Same\\\\n    pattern as verbosity (D013). Register-formality 50% agreement refutes Dream reviewer\\\\n    concern about axis overlap (r≈0.7 speculation). C3 now has 3 viable axes (formality\\\\n    88%, verbosity 86%, register 95% all NLI-only) + 1 structural failure (tone 65%).\\\\n    Register full pipeline awaits API key recovery.\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-008\\\\n    role: pilot\\\\n    result: NLI-only 95% PASS, joint gate 20% FAIL, register-formality orthogonal\\\\n      (50%)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D013\\\\n  - D014\\\\n- id: D020\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 00:42 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Dream 2 analysis: best 3.5/median 3.0/worst 3.0. Three structural fixes\\\\n    needed (causal language, RATE differentiation, psychometric references). Actual\\\\n    exp-014 data (p=0.010) much stronger than dream''s median imagination (p=0.11).\\\\n    Proceed with fixes + experiments, re-dream after framing update.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Three-tier consistent issues: (1) \\\\\\\"Causal\\\\\\\" language overclaims — all\\\\n    tiers want \\\\\\\"interventional/counterfactual-based\\\\\\\"; (2) RATE differentiation underdeveloped\\\\n    — RATE uses Likert ATE which we show is insensitive; (3) Missing psychometric\\\\n    refs (Thurstone 1927, Kiritchenko 2017, Novikova 2018, Preference Leakage). Two-tier:\\\\n    binarized Likert 1/9 cells (extend to all when data available), multiple comparisons\\\\n    correction, power analysis for null findings. Data-dependent concerns (original-text\\\\n    confound undermines C1) are mitigated by actual exp-014 showing p=0.010 GEE after\\\\n    controlling — much stronger than dream''s imagined p=0.11. Register 3rd axis (95%\\\\n    NLI) also not known to dream. Actual paper should score above dream''s median.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: extend\\\\n    result: need binarized Likert for all 9 cells\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: actual p=0.010 vs dream imagined p=0.11\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n  - D016\\\\n  - D017\\\\n  - D018\\\\n  - D019\\\\n- id: D021\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 01:04 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'exp-013 LLM-as-annotator: kappa=0.43 (kappa paradox), precision=98.9%.\\\\n    Frame as precision-oriented conservative filter, not human validation.'\\\\n  rationale: 'kappa=0.43 is below 0.6 threshold but misleading due to extreme base\\\\n    rate skew (95 YES vs 5 NO). Standard kappa paradox (Feinstein & Cicchetti 1990).\\\\n    Precision 98.9% = NLI gate almost never passes bad pairs. FNR 8.4% = conservative\\\\n    filter loses some valid pairs but exp-012 confirms no systematic bias in discards.\\\\n    Key corrections: (1) rename from \\\\\\\"human validation\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\"LLM-as-annotator validation\\\\\\\",\\\\n    (2) use standard Precision/Recall not custom FPR/FNR, (3) acknowledge Qwen3-32B\\\\n    is both rewriter and validator (evaluator-producer bias limitation), (4) plan\\\\n    GPT-4o spot check (20 pairs) when API available.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp013_nli_validation\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: kappa=0.43, precision=98.9%, recall=91.6%, agreement=91%\\\\n  - exp_id: exp012_consistency_bias\\\\n    role: supporting\\\\n    result: no systematic bias in NLI-filtered vs unfiltered pairs\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D017\\\\n- id: D022\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 01:16 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Register n=100 H1 PASS: NLI-only 94% (Wilson CI [0.875, 0.972]), pilot\\\\n    prediction accurate. C3 now has 3 working axes.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Register axis content verification on n=100 confirms pilot result (95%→94%).\\\\n    Wilson CI lower bound 87.5% > 80% threshold, resolving pilot''s CI warning (76.4%).\\\\n    Axis viability: Register 94% ≈ Formality 88% > Verbosity 86% >> Tone 65%. C3 has\\\\n    3 verified content-preserving axes (formality, verbosity, register) + 1 structural\\\\n    failure (tone). Register-formality orthogonality 50% (D019). All three axes now\\\\n    blocked on API for scoring. Pipeline: CF gen ✅ → NLI verification ✅ → scoring\\\\n    ❌ (API 402).'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: register_pilot\\\\n    role: pilot\\\\n    result: NLI 95% n=20\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-008\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: NLI 94% n=100, Wilson CI [0.875, 0.972]\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D019\\\\n- id: D023\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 01:57 UTC\\\\n  summary: Benchmark formality adopts NLI-only gating (same as verbosity/register).\\\\n    AlpacaEval 86%, MT-Bench 91% NLI-only vs 20%/32.5% joint gate.\\\\n  rationale: 'BERTScore structurally incompatible with style transfer on longer texts\\\\n    — penalizes expected vocabulary changes. Pattern identical across all axes: formality\\\\n    (LLMBar short texts OK, AlpacaEval/MT-Bench long texts fail), verbosity (D013),\\\\n    register (D019). NLI-only pass rates: AlpacaEval 86%, MT-Bench 91%, both above\\\\n    80% threshold. Code fix: extend NLI-only gate to formality axis in content_verification.py.\\\\n    No re-verification needed — NLI scores already in verified_*.jsonl, downstream\\\\n    filters by nli_score >= 0.90.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-002\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: AlpacaEval NLI-only 86%, MT-Bench NLI-only 91%\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n  - D013\\\\n  - D019\\\\n- id: D024\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:06 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Dream 3 regression: best 3.0/6 (down from 3.5), median 3.0/6, worst weak\\\\n    reject. Best tier was simulated (reduced reliability). Real review 2.5/5 takes\\\\n    priority.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Dream 3 (dream_20260521T010111) with D020 fixes scored lower than Dream\\\\n    2 — best dropped 3.5→3.0. However best tier had review_quality=simulated (single\\\\n    session, not full roundtable), reducing its reliability. Key Dream 3 issues overlap\\\\n    with real review: verbosity single-cell, Holm-Bonferroni not shown, zero figures,\\\\n    novelty ceiling. The real Round 1 review (2.5/5 Borderline Findings) is now the\\\\n    primary reference for prioritization. Dream scores are secondary.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: dream_20260521T010111\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: best 3.0/6, median 3.0/6, worst weak reject\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D020\\\\n- id: D025\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: Round 1 审稿 Action Matrix 定稿：保留 Blindspot（两层机制防御）、BT 升级 primary、加 DAG、RATE\\\\n    head-to-head 不弱化\\\\n  rationale: '基于 Reviewer 独立审视的 4 个关键修正：(1) W2 Blindspot framing: 两层机制（60% ties structural\\\\n    loss + 去 ties 后仍弱 8.5pp construct difference）使 Blindspot 可防御，审稿人 \\\\\\\"n=500 就好\\\\\\\" 只解第一层；(2)\\\\n    W8 RATE: mvp_32b_ate vs pairwise_32b 已是 matched comparison，不需弱化；(3) W17 BT: 升级为\\\\n    primary analysis，使用全部 pairwise data 含 inconsistent pairs，同时解决 43% data loss concern；(4)\\\\n    W3 DAG: 3-node DAG 成本极低 ROI 极高。19 个 issue 中 16 个已 in_progress，3 个依赖未到手数据。CLMM\\\\n    existential test 在 Agent 队列中。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: binarized Likert p=0.296 confirms two-layer mechanism\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-011\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: NLI 0.70-0.95 all p<0.005, threshold robustness confirmed\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-012\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: no systematic bias in consistency filtering\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-013\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: NLI validation precision 98.9%, PABAK 0.82\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-014\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: formality OR=2.21 p=0.010, orig_pref OR=1.82 p=0.052\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D020\\\\n  - D024\\\\n- id: D026\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:27 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'CLMM existential test PASS: OrderedModel p=0.769, Wilcoxon p=0.905 — Likert\\\\n    Blindspot 完全确认，ordinal correction 无法挽救'\\\\n  rationale: 'OrderedModel (ordinal logistic, no random effects) on NLI≥0.90 subset\\\\n    (n=88 pairs, 176 obs): is_formal coef=-0.079 p=0.769, is_original coef=-0.090\\\\n    p=0.735. Wilcoxon p=0.905. CLMM 比 ATE (p=0.332) 更不显著——62.5% ties 是任何 Likert 方法的结构性限制。is_formal\\\\n    系数方向为负（formal lower scores）与 pairwise 69.1% prefer formal 方向相反，支持 absolute scoring\\\\n    和 forced comparison 测量不同构念。审稿人 W2/CROSS-4 的 \\\\\\\"如果 CLMM 显著则 claim 被推翻\\\\\\\" 完全排除。可以安全推进两层\\\\n    Blindspot framing。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp_32b_ate\\\\n    role: data_source\\\\n    result: scored_32b.jsonl Likert data\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: comparison\\\\n    result: 69.1% p=0.006\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: comparison\\\\n    result: binarized 60.6% p=0.296\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D025\\\\n- id: D027\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:30 UTC\\\\n  summary: BT 分析完成：formal win prob 61.9% [55.1%, 68.8%] p=0.001 on ALL 176 comparisons\\\\n    — 比 filtered sign test 更显著，同时解决 data loss concern\\\\n  rationale: 'BT model (choix ILSR) on all 176 pairwise comparisons (88 pairs × 2\\\\n    trials, NLI≥0.90, including 42 inconsistent pairs): formal strength=0.243, casual=-0.243,\\\\n    diff=0.487, bootstrap 95% CI [0.205, 0.789], p=0.001. Win probability 61.9% [55.1%,\\\\n    68.8%]. Comparison: consistency-filtered sign test 73.9% (34/46) p=0.006 — BT\\\\n    slightly lower win rate but compensated by 4× more data and even more significant.\\\\n    Validates that consistency filter does not inflate the finding. Addresses W14\\\\n    (data loss), W17 (BT), R1-W2 (filter bias) simultaneously. Reviewer suggested\\\\n    BT as primary analysis; results support this.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: data_source\\\\n    result: 176 comparisons, 109 formal wins\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-012\\\\n    role: confirmed\\\\n    result: consistency filter no bias, now BT confirms no inflation\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D025\\\\n  - D026\\\\n- id: D028\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:40 UTC\\\\n  summary: CLMM→ordinal logistic regression 命名修正 + BT bootstrap pair-level fix\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 审计发现：(1) exp-015 使用 OrderedModel 无随机效应，是 CLM 非 CLMM，论文中必须准确称呼\\\\n    ordinal logistic regression / proportional odds model；(2) exp-016 BT bootstrap\\\\n    在 comparison 级别重采样但 trial1/trial2 共享 pair，需改为 pair-level resampling，否则 CI 偏窄。结论方向不受影响（p=0.769\\\\n    修正后更大；BT CI 即使稍宽仍排除 50%），但术语和统计正确性是必须的。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-015\\\\n    role: target\\\\n    result: CLM naming fix needed\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: target\\\\n    result: bootstrap unit fix needed\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D026\\\\n  - D027\\\\n- id: D029\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:41 UTC\\\\n  summary: Ordinal regression 无 RE 是反保守检验（加强 Blindspot 结论）+ 方向反转解读降调 + BT 主分析用 NLI-filtered\\\\n    子集\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 验证三个关键统计学判断：(1) 无随机效应的 OrderedModel SE 偏低→p 偏小→反保守，在最有利条件下仍\\\\n    p=0.769 加强 Blindspot 结论；(2) is_formal coef=-0.079 CI[-0.60,0.45] 横跨零点，不可做方向推断，\\\\\\\"different\\\\n    constructs\\\\\\\"假说移至 Discussion；(3) BT 主分析用 NLI≥0.90 (176 comparisons) 与其他分析一致，全量数据\\\\n    (197) 作 robustness check。四种方法（ordinal/GEE/Wilcoxon/ATE）在三个维度交叉全部不显著，不需要第五种 GEE\\\\n    ordinal。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-015\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: p=0.769 anti-conservative\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: NLI-filtered 176 as primary, all-data 197 as robustness\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D026\\\\n  - D027\\\\n  - D028\\\\n- id: D030\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:51 UTC\\\\n  summary: Power curve 修正：tie rate + consistency filter + Hoenig framing。修正后加强 Blindspot\\\\n    论证\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 发现 power curve 两个 critical bugs：(1) binarized Likert 未计入 62.5%\\\\n    tie rate，80% power 从 n≈172 修正为 n≈464；(2) pairwise 未计入 43% consistency filter loss。同时图使用\\\\n    observed effect sizes 与论文 Hoenig & Heisey 声明矛盾——改 framing 为 illustrative sensitivity\\\\n    comparison。所有修正使 sensitivity gap 更大，加强而非削弱 Blindspot 论证。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-010\\\\n    role: data_source\\\\n    result: binarized 60.6%, tie_rate 62.5%\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: data_source\\\\n    result: BT 60.9% as alternative pairwise effect size\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D029\\\\n- id: D031\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 02:52 UTC\\\\n  summary: 全文数字统一：BT 62% 为 primary headline，退役 69.1%，sign test 74% 为 secondary\\\\n  rationale: 论文中存在三个不同的 formal preference 数字（69.1% 旧分析含 NLI<0.90、73.9% NLI≥0.90 consistency-filtered、61.9%\\\\n    BT NLI≥0.90 全量），造成混乱。统一为 BT 62% 作为 primary（最可防御：无 consistency filter、proper parametric\\\\n    model），sign test 74% 作为 secondary confirmatory，all-data BT 61% 作为 robustness。69.1%\\\\n    完全退役——来自混合数据子集，不应出现在论文中。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: BT 61.9% NLI≥0.90\\\\n  - exp_id: pairwise_32b\\\\n    role: secondary\\\\n    result: sign test 73.9% NLI≥0.90 consistent\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D027\\\\n  - D029\\\\n- id: D032\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 03:32 UTC\\\\n  summary: 最终 canonical BT 数字：63.0% [55.8%, 70.3%] p<0.001（173 comparisons, 88 pairs,\\\\n    NLI≥0.90, pair-level bootstrap 10000x）\\\\n  rationale: BT pair-level bootstrap 修复后数字从 61.9% 变为 63.0%。差异来源：(1) 3 个无效 trial 被正确排除（173\\\\n    vs 176 comparisons）；(2) pair-level resampling 的 CI 比 comparison-level 宽 2-5%。All-data\\\\n    BT 60.9% [53.8%, 67.8%] 作为 robustness check。Sign test 73.9% (34/46 NLI≥0.90 consistent)\\\\n    作为 secondary confirmatory。69.1% 和 61.9% 均正式退役。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: 63.0% [55.8%, 70.3%] p<0.001, 173 comparisons\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D031\\\\n  - D028\\\\n- id: D033\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 04:11 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Claim framing: 机制性 \\\\\\\"structural limitation\\\\\\\" 可说，量化 ratio 不进 headline，Qwen3-32B\\\\n    local judge 是必做的 1→2 judge 跨越'\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 独立评估：(1) 62.5% tie rate 是 integer Likert 的数学必然，机制性声明有理论+实证双重支撑；(2)\\\\n    24× ratio cherry-picks 端点（BT/corrected=6.7×），且与 Hoenig 声明矛盾，不宜 headline 化；(3)\\\\n    Qwen3-32B (open-source) vs GPT-4o (proprietary) 是最大差异度配对，跨过 \\\\\\\"observation → pattern\\\\\\\"\\\\n    门槛。关键预测指标：Qwen3-32B tie rate 是否在 50-70% 范围（支持机制普遍性）。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-015\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: ordinal p=0.769 排除 interval-scale artifact\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-016\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: BT 63.0% 6-method hierarchy\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D032\\\\n- id: D034\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 04:28 UTC\\\\n  summary: Qwen3-32B 确认 Blindspot 跨 2 judges × 2 axes。Verbosity 87.3% 为最强效应。Paper\\\\n    升级为 multi-judge multi-axis 叙事\\\\n  rationale: Qwen3-32B (open-source) 在 formality (76.4% pairwise, Likert p=0.908)\\\\n    和 verbosity (87.3%, Likert p=0.179) 上均确认 Blindspot。Register 为 negative control\\\\n    (59.3% p=0.220)。Tie rates 跨 4 个配置在 58-73% 范围，支持结构性机制。论文从 single-judge 升级为 \\\\\\\"across\\\\n    architecturally distinct judges\\\\\\\"。需注意 evaluator-producer bias (Qwen3-32B = rewriter\\\\n    + judge)，但 GPT-4o 独立 judge 同方向确认缓解此 concern。Verbosity 两个方向均偏好 verbose，是最 clean\\\\n    的 Blindspot 案例。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_formality\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 76.4% pairwise, Likert p=0.908, tie rate 72.7%\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_verbosity\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 87.3% pairwise, Likert p=0.179, tie rate 58.1%\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_register\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 59.3% p=0.220, negative control\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D033\\\\n- id: D035\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 04:37 UTC\\\\n  summary: Qwen3-32B BT + GEE 完成：BT formality 66.5% p<0.0001, verbosity 77.3% p<0.0001;\\\\n    GEE register significant after originality control (OR=1.91 p=0.046); Qwen3-32B\\\\n    originality bias 比 GPT-4o 强 ~2x\\\\n  rationale: 'BT pair-level bootstrap 10000x 确认 Qwen3-32B 的 formality 和 verbosity\\\\n    bias。GEE register 分离出极强 originality bias (OR=5.72 p<0.0001) 后 register style effect\\\\n    勉强显著 (OR=1.91 p=0.046)，将 Blindspot 覆盖从 4/6 cells 升级到 5/6。Qwen3-32B formality GEE:\\\\n    formal OR=4.20 p=0.0002 vs GPT-4o OR=2.21 p=0.010，originality OR=4.70 vs 1.82\\\\n    — evaluator-producer bias 使两个效应都膨胀约 2x，但方向一致。Register p=0.046 刚过门槛，论文中需谨慎表述为 marginally\\\\n    significant / exploratory。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_formality\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: BT 66.5% [58.5%, 73.9%] p<0.0001; GEE formal OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality\\\\n      OR=4.70 p<0.0001\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_verbosity\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: BT 77.3% [70.3%, 84.3%] p<0.0001\\\\n  - exp_id: qwen32b_register\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: GEE academic OR=1.91 [1.01, 3.58] p=0.046; originality OR=5.72 [3.02,\\\\n      10.82] p<0.0001\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D034\\\\n- id: D036\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 05:30 UTC\\\\n  summary: GPT-4o verbosity 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ + register 63.3% p=0.085 (NS)。跨模型验证 verbosity\\\\n    bias，register 两个 judge 都不显著\\\\n  rationale: GPT-4o verbosity 86.3% 与 Qwen3-32B 87.3% 几乎一致（差 1pp），跨 proprietary/open-source\\\\n    架构确认 verbosity 是最强 style bias。GPT-4o register 63.3% p=0.085 与 Qwen3-32B 59.3%\\\\n    p=0.22 模式一致——两个 judge 都不显著，register 是 originality-dominated axis。Claude/Gemini\\\\n    API 不可用（代理仅支持 OpenAI），多 judge 扩展限于 GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B。Likert ATE 分析待 P0 worker\\\\n    完成\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-020\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: GPT-4o verbosity 86.3% p<1e-6, register 63.3% p=0.085 NS\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D035\\\\n- id: D037\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 05:34 UTC\\\\n  summary: GPT-4o 完整统计分析完成：Verbosity BT 76.0% p=0.0001 + Likert p=0.403 → Blindspot\\\\n    confirmed。Register BT 57.0% p=0.04。6/6 Blindspot cells (4 strong + 2 marginal\\\\n    register)。跨 judge GEE gradient 完美复现\\\\n  rationale: P0 统计分析 6 项全部完成。GPT-4o verbosity Blindspot 是关键缺失数据点，现已确认（BT 76.0% vs\\\\n    Likert p=0.403）。跨 judge verbosity OR 高度一致（10.97 vs 13.10），且两个 judge 的 originality\\\\n    都 NS——verbosity 是唯一 confound-free axis。GPT-4o register BT 57.0% p=0.04（之前 sign\\\\n    test 63.3% p=0.085 是 consistency-filtered）。证据矩阵完整：4 strong Blindspot + 2 marginal\\\\n    register Blindspot。GEE gradient 跨 judge 复现。Evaluator-producer bias 与 D035 预期一致（Qwen3-32B\\\\n    originality OR 系统偏高）\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-020\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: GPT-4o Likert ATE + BT + GEE complete for verbosity and register\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D036\\\\n- id: D038\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 05:57 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'Qwen3-32B register BT pair-level bootstrap: P=0.553, p=0.076 (NS). Evidence\\\\n    matrix corrected to \\\\\\\"4+2\\\\\\\" pattern.'\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer #24 flagged methodological inconsistency: Qwen3-32B register\\\\n    used sign test while other 5 cells used BT. Re-ran with BT pair-level bootstrap\\\\n    (10000 resamples, seed=42). Result: P(academic)=0.553 [0.479, 0.628] p=0.076 —\\\\n    not significant. This weakens register from \\\\\\\"marginal\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\"weak\\\\\\\" for Qwen3-32B,\\\\n    confirming \\\\\\\"4+2\\\\\\\" framing: 4 strong Blindspot cells (formality+verbosity × 2 judges)\\\\n    + 2 weak register cells. GEE style OR=1.91 p=0.046 still significant after controlling\\\\n    originality, consistent with register being originality-dominated axis. Forest\\\\n    plot regenerated with all 6 rows using consistent BT methodology.'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: exp-019\\\\n    role: source_data\\\\n    result: Qwen3-32B register BT 55.3% p=0.076 NS\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D037\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 29688, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01En36V24Y5wN7AVuRMBbnW2","session_id":"c31a7728-a7db-4599-bbbd-5af253d1fc6a","uuid":"f7e158a8-ad02-4174-9963-d7aa3f6edc48","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:59:23.891Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HRaYvKkgtgzazR7wybxess","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UNEUGvXnmw2K2aSLDMbLND","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"causal_style_decomp_judge","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19936,"cache_read_input_tokens":19324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19936,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01En36V24Y5wN7AVuRMBbnW2","session_id":"c31a7728-a7db-4599-bbbd-5af253d1fc6a","uuid":"3d1b310b-ae6a-4e5f-a13b-277ff5815588"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNEUGvXnmw2K2aSLDMbLND","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\\\\n\\\\n> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\\\\n> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\\\\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\\\\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\\\\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\\\\n\\\\n## Title\\\\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\\\\n\\\\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\\\\n- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\\\\n- 状态：✅ 4/6 cells 强显著 + 2 weak register (\\\\\\\"4+2\\\\\\\" pattern)\\\\n- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001, verbosity 76.0% p=0.0001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5% p<0.0001, verbosity 77.3% p<0.0001; register: GPT-4o 57.0% p=0.04 marginal, Qwen3-32B 55.3% p=0.076 NS\\\\n\\\\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\\\\n- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\\\\n- 状态：✅ 4/4 strong cells confirmed (formality + verbosity × 2 judges: BT all p<0.001 while Likert all NS)\\\\n- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\\\\n- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\\\\n- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\\\\n\\\\n### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\\\\n- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\\\\n- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\\\\n- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\\\\n\\\\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\\\\n- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\\\\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\\\\n- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\\\\n\\\\n## Evidence Matrix (D037 — COMPLETE)\\\\n\\\\n| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Blindspot |\\\\n|---|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\\\\n| **Formality** | 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<.0001 / p=.908 | ✅ Strong |\\\\n| **Verbosity** | 76.0% [66.7, 85.3] p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<.0001 / p=.179 | ✅ Strong |\\\\n| **Register** | 57.0% [46.8, 63.9] p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% [47.9, 62.8] p=.076 / p=.505 | ⚠️ Weak |\\\\n\\\\n**4+2 Blindspot pattern**: 4 strong (formality + verbosity, both judges) + 2 weak register (GPT-4o marginal p=.04, Qwen3-32B NS p=.076)\\\\n\\\\n**GEE Cross-Judge Gradient** (完美复现):\\\\n\\\\n| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3-32B Style OR | Qwen3-32B Orig OR |\\\\n|------|-----------------|----------------|--------------------|--------------------|\\\\n| Verbosity | **10.97** p<.0001 | 0.44 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\\\\n| Formality | 2.21 p=.010 | 1.82 NS | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\\\\n| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\\\\n\\\\nGradient: Verbosity (pure style, confound-free) > Formality (mixed) > Register (originality-dominated)\\\\nEvaluator-producer bias: Qwen3-32B originality OR systematically higher (~2×) than GPT-4o\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n### Problem\\\\nLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\\\\n\\\\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\\\\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\\\\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\\\\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\\\\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\\\\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\\\\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\\\\n\\\\n### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\\\\n用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\\\\n核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\\\\nGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\\\\n\\\\n**语言规范**：\\\\n- \\\\\\\"interventional\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"counterfactual-based measurement\\\\\\\"（非 \\\\\\\"causal\\\\\\\"）\\\\n- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\\\\n- 全文已降调因果术语\\\\n\\\\n### Headline Result\\\\n\\\\\\\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\\\\n\\\\n19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\\\\n\\\\n**Effectively resolved**:\\\\n- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\\\\n- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\\\\n- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\\\\n- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\\\\n\\\\n**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\\\\n- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\\\\n- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\\\\n- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\\\\n- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\\\\n- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\\\\n- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\\\\n- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\\\\n- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\\\\n\\\\n**Gaps remaining**:\\\\n- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\\\\n- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\\\\n- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\\\\n- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\\\\n- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\\\\n\\\\n## Figures (3 — ALL COMPLETE)\\\\n1. **Power curve** — ✅ BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\\\\n2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers (39.9KB PDF)\\\\n3. **Forest plot** — ✅ 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI (24KB PDF)\\\\n\\\\n## Bibliography\\\\n22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\\\\n证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 6952, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01En36V24Y5wN7AVuRMBbnW2","session_id":"c31a7728-a7db-4599-bbbd-5af253d1fc6a","uuid":"6d37bed3-650e-4fc4-bd68-75edc2a47a0b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:59:29.190Z"}
